  m_text: 'Perspective depends only on where the camera stands. The Field of View only crops the picture: a smaller angle shows a smaller part of the same view.


    <b>Predict:</b> Two cameras look down the lamp rows. One stands far back with Field of View 25; the other stands close with Field of View 70. The first posts are the same size in both. How do the posts behind them look in each picture?


    <b>Try:</b> Match the spacing of the lamps in reference 22. Choose where the camera stands first, then set the Field of View.


    <size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Reference 22</color></size>'
