  m_text: 'A smooth surface shows a picture of its surroundings taken from somewhere else: the sky, or the nearest Reflection Probe. A probe is a cubemap captured from one point and used by the objects inside its box. This one is baked (Type: Custom).


    <b>Predict:</b> Two identical arcades on a wet floor. A has no probe; B has a Reflection Probe. What does each floor reflect?


    <b>Try:</b> Move the camera sideways and watch B''s reflections with the probe''s Box Projection off, then on.


    <size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Materials training E</color></size>'
